## SQ-DEP-09b
@group A
@commands One throwaway boot per mod, each with only that jar removed from `srv/mods/`: buzzier_bees, corn_delight, create_factory, fruitsdelight, hostiledelight, moredelight, supplementaries, upgrade_aquatic, quark, immersiveengineering. If Forge refuses ("Missing or unsupported mandatory dependencies") because another jar requires it, record SKIP (cascade) with the requiring jars and move on. Known cascades (r1115): supplementaries <- suppsquared; upgrade_aquatic <- alexsabnormalities; quark <- quarkengineering (and with it removed too, Botania still needs Quark's API); immersiveengineering <- quarkengineering, more_immersive_wires, compressedengineering, controlengineering, immersiveposts, immersivepetroleum, kubejs_immersive_engineering, tmted. Per boot: `grep -nE "$ERR" logs/latest.log \| grep -i <mod>`; `/datapack list enabled \| grep creativedelight:mods/`; for corn_delight, create_factory, upgrade_aquatic also `/loot spawn ~ ~ ~ loot hearthandharvest:chests/corn_maze` (or `creativedelight:gameplay/fishing_net/junk`) x5
@pass `Done (`; no ERR line naming the removed mod; its `creativedelight:mods/<mod>` pack is not listed; the loot spawns still give items (at most a `Found validation problem ... Unknown loot table called <ns>:mod_items/<mod>/...` WARN); for moredelight / hostiledelight no `placed_omelette` / `placed_suspicious_bacon_and_eggs` block (`/setblock` fails)
@fails the ERR file is the next one to guard: run `python3 tools/optional_ref_audit.py --all` and check why it was not flagged (namespace map, closure); recipe errors: missing `forge:mod_loaded` on that recipe
@draft one throwaway boot per removed jar (10 boots, cascades recorded as SKIP by hand): a runner loop outside one batch; per boot the checks are those of SQ-DEP-02 (rerun 5.2) with the removed mod in the greps
